# =============================================================================
# Toolchain recipe — example template for custom/ units (toolchain sets)
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is an inert template: every line stays commented, so discovery
# sees no toolchain here. To write your own toolchain, copy this file to
# custom/<id>.Dockerfile (id: lowercase [a-z0-9-], 'base' is reserved),
# remove the leading '# ' markers, and adapt the commands.
#
# Grammar (lint-enforced at discovery, build and editor save):
#   - Allowed directives: RUN, ENV, USER, comments, and
#     '# extra: <absolute path>' lines (files the payload dump must capture
#     because dpkg/pip do not know them — e.g. manual /etc writes, npm
#     globals, tar-extracted binaries).
#   - ARG, COPY, WORKDIR and ENTRYPOINT are refused: ARG hides out-of-band
#     state from the content hash, COPY has no build context, and the
#     composition footer owns the rest.
#   - USER switching is monotonic root -> dev; only root and dev exist. The
#     fragment runs as root unless you switch.
#   - Every install is pinned: pip needs ==x.y.z, npm needs @x.y.z, direct
#     download URLs must embed the exact version (no 'latest'), rustup needs
#     --default-toolchain <version>. apt is exempt — its pin is the suite.
#   - ENV PATH is refused: PATH additions go into ~/.profile.d/<id>.sh.
#     Direct writes to ~/.profile or ~/.bashrc are refused too.
#
# This file lives in custom/ and is kept across updates (recreated from this
# template when absent). Its name deliberately does not end in .Dockerfile —
# discovery registers exactly the custom/<id>.Dockerfile files, so this
# template stays inert.
#
# =============================================================================
# Example: a custom toolchain "example" (copy to example.Dockerfile to use)
# =============================================================================
#
# USER root
#
# # --- apt packages (apt is exempt from pin enforcement) ----------------------
# RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
#         hello \
#     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
#
# # --- pip packages (exact pins required) --------------------------------------
# RUN pip3 install --break-system-packages --no-cache-dir \
#         requests==2.32.3
#
# # --- npm globals (exact pins required; declare module + bin as extras) -------
# RUN npm install -g markdown-it@14.1.0
#
# # --- PATH additions ride the ~/.profile.d hook, never ENV PATH ----------------
# RUN mkdir -p ~/.profile.d \
#     && printf 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"\n' > ~/.profile.d/example.sh
#
# USER dev
